  "query_preview": "..\nA long elongated trough connecting all the way into Typhoon In-fa \nhas weakened slightly from last night and is starting to drift south.\nThis feature is now expected to bring scattered showers and isolated\nthunderstorms to Tinian and Saipan early tonight, Rota all night, \nand Guam by late tonight. Isolated showers will return once the \ntrough has passed each island. Isolated showers will likely continue \nfor much of the forecast period for Guam and Rota. Scattered showers \nand isolated thunderstorms may return Friday for Tinian and Saipan \ndue to slightly closer proximity to In-fa as passes somewhere through\nthe far northern CNMI between Sarigan and Maug. Showers for Tinian \nand Saipan will likely return to isolated for the rest of the \nforecast period by Saturday. Current Typhoon In-Fa is expected to \nmake it's closest point of approach midday Friday. Breezy conditions \nare possible for Tinian and Saipan Friday with frequent gusts of 30 \nmph, particularly in thunderstorms. This situation will continue to \nbe monitored closely for any potential changes. See the \"Tropical \nSystems\" section for more details.",
